{
 "_provenance": {
  "experiment": "Matched-initialization protocol extended from the crowd-sourced-annotation control to the full section 5.3 PPLBench comparison suite: logistic_regression, robust_regression, n_schools, noisy_or_topic (NUTS, all four frameworks), plus a Stan ADVI matched-init attempt on the three VI models. One-stop dataset for the comparison subsection.",
  "date": "2026-07-14",
  "protocol_statement": "Every experiment in the comparison subsection starts from the same initial state where the framework allows it. The canonical init point is the constrained image of unconstrained zeros under the standard transforms: real-support sites at 0, positive-support sites at 1 (exp transform in all four systems), simplex sites at uniform (centered stick-breaking maps 0 to uniform), Gumbel sites (real support) at 0. Standard PPLBench protocol otherwise unchanged: iterations 4000, warmup 1000, 4 trials (trials-as-chains), model seed 12345, step_size 0.1, max_tree_depth 10, dense mass adaptation, cpu, 32 threads.",
  "init_point_per_model": {
   "logistic_regression": "alpha = 0, beta = zeros(k) (all real).",
   "robust_regression": "alpha = 0, beta = zeros(k) (real); nu = 1, sigma = 1 (positive, exp transform).",
   "n_schools": "sigma_state = sigma_district = sigma_type = 1 (positive, exp transform); beta_baseline = 0, beta_state = beta_district(_flat) = beta_type = 0 (real).",
   "noisy_or_topic": "active_gumbel_true = active_gumbel_false = zeros(1+num_topics) (Gumbel support is all of R).",
   "crowd_sourced_annotation": "prev and every confusion row = uniform simplex ones(K)/K (stick-breaking image of 0)."
  },
  "mechanism_per_system": {
   "impulse": "build_constraint in standard/<model>.jl pins the latents to the canonical point; the constraint feeds ProbProg.generate in harness.jl nuts_program, so the NUTS chain starts there deterministically for every trial. For logistic/robust/n_schools the per-trial Uniform(-2,2) init_params from the upstream generate_init_params is now intentionally ignored (2026-07-14 change); annotation and noisy-or were already deterministic.",
   "numpyro": "impl.matched_init_params(data) returns the constrained canonical dict; numpyro_harness.py converts it to unconstrained z via numpyro.infer.init_to_value (verified max|z| = 0) and passes init_params=z to mcmc.run for EVERY trial. Matched init overrides the driver's per-trial init_params (harness precedence fixed 2026-07-14).",
   "stan": "impl.matched_init_params(data) returns the constrained canonical dict; stan_harness.py passes it as CmdStan `inits` (constrained scale) for every trial, overriding driver per-trial inits.",
   "turing": "turing/standard/<model>.jl matched_init_params(data) returns a constrained NamedTuple; turing_harness.jl passes it via DynamicPPL.InitFromParams as sample()'s initial_params for every trial (server loop keeps the fixed matched init, ignoring driver per-trial inits).",
   "stan_advi": "cmdstanpy CmdStanModel.variational(inits=<constrained canonical dict>) per trial; opt-in via svi/*_matched_init.json configs."
  },
  "impulse_rerun_reason": {
   "logistic_regression": "case (b): default protocol fed a per-trial Uniform(-2,2) prior-ish draw from generate_init_params; now pinned to canonical.",
   "robust_regression": "case (b): same, plus nu/sigma exp(Uniform(-2,2)) draws; now pinned (nu=1, sigma=1; old fallback was nu=20, sigma=10).",
   "n_schools": "case (b): same (sigmas exp(Uniform(-2,2))); now pinned (sigmas=1).",
   "noisy_or_topic": "init already canonical (case a: zeros, deterministic) but the arm HAD to re-run because the model itself was fixed 2026-07-14 (missing `+ aw` term in the Gumbel-softmax logit, standard/noisy_or_topic.jl line 64); old numbers targeted a different posterior.",
   "crowd_sourced_annotation": "case (a): already canonical (uniform simplices); NOT re-run."
  },
  "default_init_references": {
   "logistic_robust_nschools": "NumPyro/Impulse/Stan: paper_data_G4_2026-07-06_052754.json (run G4); Turing.jl: paper_data_G5_2026-07-06_200311.json (run G5; robust and n_schools G5 Turing arms ran only 1-2 valid trials, see caveats).",
   "noisy_or": "Impulse/Stan: paper_data_G4 (INVALID: pre-bug-fix model); NumPyro/Turing.jl: discrete_missing_arms_results_2026-07-13.json.",
   "stan_advi": "svi_stan_turing_results_2026-07-13.json.",
   "annotation": "annotation_matched_init_results_2026-07-14.json (imported wholesale under annotation_import)."
  },
  "caveats": [
   "Turing.jl robust_regression and n_schools default-init references (G5) pooled ESS over only 2 trials (one valid wall time each); the matched-init n_eff/s gains there (57.5->279.1 and 17.1->57.9) are roughly 2x from the 2-vs-4 pooled-chain count and 2x from the init policy; per-trial wall times are comparable (robust 95s->72-90s, n_schools 241s->265-291s). PLLs in band.",
   "Impulse noisy-or old-vs-new is NOT an init comparison: the old model was buggy (different target). See impulse_noisy_or_fix.",
   "The three standard models are essentially unimodal: matched-init moved NumPyro/Stan medians <10% and Impulse <15%, as expected."
  ],
